{
  "$comment": [
    "THE RIBBON, AS DATA -- decision D1-8 (Stage1-AppShell-Plan.md 3).",
    "",
    "This file is the whole ribbon. ui/shell/RibbonTabBuilder builds every tab, group and button",
    "from it and from core/cmd/ActionRegistry, and there is no widget code anywhere that places a",
    "command. That is the property worth protecting: adding a command in Stage 9 must be a registry",
    "row plus a line here, because the instant a typo yields a silently missing button instead of an",
    "error, the next person writes widget code and this mechanism becomes dead weight that still has",
    "to be maintained.",
    "",
    "So it is VALIDATED AT BUILD TIME by tools/ribbon-validate, which fails the build on an unknown",
    "action id, a duplicate placement, or an empty group, naming the id and the line. The validator",
    "and the runtime builder share one parser (ui/shell/RibbonModel) -- see that header for why two",
    "would be worse than none.",
    "",
    "FIELDS. tab.title and group.title are CATALOG KEYS, not text: this project's catalog key IS the",
    "source string (T6), so English lives in i18n/rawpage_en.ts like every other locale.",
    "collapsePriority is HIGHER-COLLAPSES-FIRST, and it is deliberately not the same axis as visual",
    "order -- the least important group folds into a popup button first, while Tab still has to visit",
    "the groups left to right. Conflating the two is issue I-05, found by walking the spike.",
    "",
    "SCOPE AT STAGE 1. Every id below is DECLARED in ActionId.def; almost none is REGISTERED yet, and",
    "an unregistered id renders as a visible, disabled button whose tooltip names the stage it",
    "arrives in. That is the honest state and it is the point of placing them now: the ribbon's",
    "shape, sizing and collapse behaviour are exercised at their real width from Stage 1 rather than",
    "growing under us for thirteen stages."
  ],

